<!--
    GH-874: an ARM function that returns a constant through a conditional
    return and otherwise tail-calls printed void.

      pick:    cmp r0,#0; moveq r0,#7; bxeq lr; b getv
      pair:    the same with a 64-bit 7 (moveq r0,#7; moveq r1,#0), so the
               value written first passes two merges that re-test Z
      popr:    push {r11,lr}; bl getv; cmp r0,#0; moveq r0,#3;
               popeq {r11,pc}; pop {r11,lr}; b getv
      tpick:   pick in Thumb (itt eq; moveq r0,#7; bxeq lr; b.w getvt)
      differ:  the return tests r1, not r0 (cmp r1,#0; bxeq lr), so the 7
               reaches getv when a0 == 0 and a1 != 0
      stores:  streq r0,[r1] stores the 7 on the path that returns it
      compl:   the return is inverted (bxne lr), so the 7 only reaches getv
      spin:    cmp r0,#0; moveq r0,#7; beq 1f; str r0,[r1]; bx lr; 1: b 1b
      nrexit:  cmp r0,#0; moveq r0,#7; bleq exit; str r0,[r1]; bx lr
      tnrexit: nrexit in Thumb (itt eq; moveq r0,#7; bleq abort)

    Conditional execution leaves a merge block that branches on Z again, so
    in the graph the 7 reaches both the RETURN and the tail call, though
    the execution that wrote it always returns.  ActionConditionalExe
    threads that block only after ActionReturnRecovery scored the output
    trials, and onlyOpUse rejected r0 for the competing CALL use.  With
    condexeretuse on, a use the merge rules out is skipped.  In differ the
    7 can reach getv, in stores the STORE is on the path that returns, and
    in compl the call is the only use the 7 can reach, so all three keep
    the upstream void in both passes.  In spin, nrexit and tnrexit the 7
    is forced away from the RETURN (into a spin loop or a call that does
    not return), so it never reaches it: skipping the STORE and the RETURN
    there would pass the walk with nothing checked, and all three must
    keep void too.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 "output-prototype", option condexeretuse.  Pass 1
    pins off (the bug), pass 2 the default.
-->
